    <key>NSHealthShareUsageDescription</key>
    <string>APEX reads your active energy, heart rate, HRV, VO₂ max, respiratory rate, blood oxygen, and sleep stages from Apple Health to compute recovery and biological fitness age.</string>
    <key>NSHealthUpdateUsageDescription</key>
    <string>APEX saves your completed strength workouts and active energy directly into Apple Health.</string>
    <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
    <string>APEX uses the camera with on-device Apple Vision &amp; TrueDepth to track exercise form, scan lab panels, and measure craniofacial symmetry.</string>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>APEX analyzes vocal resonance for voice biomarkers.</string>
    <key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
    <string>APEX lets you select portraits or bloodwork lab photos for on-device Apple Vision analysis.</string>
    <key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
    <string>APEX discovers your Mac Companion app over local Wi-Fi via Bonjour to synchronize Apple Health telemetry and scans privately.</string>
    <key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
    <string>APEX connects directly to Polar and Garmin BLE heart rate straps (0x180D) for real-time beat-to-beat R-R intervals and 60s HRR recovery tracking.</string>
    <key>NSMotionUsageDescription</key>
    <string>APEX uses AirPods Pro spatial head motion sensors to detect cervical forward-head posture during desk and training sessions.</string>
    <key>NSBonjourServices</key>
    <array>
        <string>_apexos._tcp</string>
    </array>
